// 128x128 or 256x64 output tile, with a 64-element reduction tile.
// Each wave reuses matrix fragments across eight output fragments.
// epilogue: 0 = F32 projection/partials; 1 = F16 GELU; 2 = F32 residual.
// Split-K writes unbiased F32 partials in separate row slabs.
// K must be divisible by 64 * splits; M must not exceed max_rows.
// Lambda is read only for the residual epilogue; other modes bind bias there.
// Input staging is zero-padded at row tails; MMA reduction order is unchanged.
